# {{ title_case_name }}

A starter Frust design system: a themed widget catalog you own, built on the
`frust` facade's public API alone — distilled from the framework's own
out-of-tree proof (`examples/design-system-sample` in the Frust repo).

## What's here

| Module | Holds |
|--------|-------|
| [`tokens`] | `design_theme()` — a `Theme` built from `Theme::neutral()` plus this system's identity tag |
| the crate root | `BadgeView`/`BadgeWidget` — one leaf widget authored against `frust::authoring`, and `install()` |

Add more widgets (a single-child container, an interactive control) the same
way — `frust::authoring` is the whole seam; nothing here reaches into
`frust-core`/`frust-widgets`/`frust-theme` directly.

## Installing

```rust
frust::app!(App, setup = {
    {{ name }}::install();
});
```

### The install-timing contract

`{{ name }}::install()` calls `frust::set_default_theme`, and it must be
called from `frust::app!`'s `setup = { .. }` block, **not** from a
`Component::init`:

- **`setup`, not `Component::init`** — `setup` runs before the shell builds
  its first frame and before any component initialises. `Component::init`
  has no kept ordering contract against the shell's own theme seeding, so a
  theme installed there may or may not be in place for frame one.
- **`set_default_theme`, not `set_app_theme`** — `set_app_theme` is the
  app-facing *override* and it pins brightness, so an app themed that way
  stops following platform light/dark. `set_default_theme` seeds the *base*
  the shell keeps re-deriving light/dark against. Precedence:
  `set_app_theme` override → `set_default_theme` base → the shell's own
  `Theme::neutral()` fallback.

## Never enable a built-in catalog feature

A design-system crate must never enable `glyph`/`material`/`cupertino` on
its `frust` dependency. Cargo features are additive and unify across a
build: one such line here turns a built-in catalog back on for *every* app
that depends on this crate, with no way for that app to switch it off
again. A design system that needs a symbol only a catalog provides has
found a gap in `frust::authoring`, not a reason to enable one. This crate's
own `Cargo.toml` ships `default-features = false` with no `features` list —
keep it that way.

